hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2849","###
 Narrated to us by Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Ghafiqi, who said: Narrated to us by Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed him that his father said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) combined the Maghrib and Isha prayers at Arafat (Jama'), with no prostration (i.e., no voluntary prayer) between them. He prayed Maghrib in three rak'ahs, then prayed Isha in two"
